Makati City, Philippines
Business AnalystLending & Trade FinanceCOO Finance – Tribe Financial Accounting
Background on what ING is about:
ING Hubs Philippines (ING Hubs PH) is an international part of the ING organization delivering services to many Business Units across the world for both Wholesale Banking and Retail Banking activities. Working for ING Hubs PH means working with the most diverse workforce and where no challenge is the same.
At ING our purpose is to empower people to stay a step ahead in life and business. We believe that sustainable progress is driven by people with the imagination and determination to make a better future for themselves and those around them.
ING is changing what banking is. For you, that means plenty of opportunities for personal growth in a continuously evolving environment. If this is the environment you thrive in, then apply and join us in changing the future of banking!
Would you like to work at the heart of the Bank’s complexity? Do you want to use your analytical and communication skills to make a difference? And would you like to have a view on the front-to-back processing chain of a large Dutch bank with an extensive international network? If this appeals to you, then the Financial Accounting Tribe is your match. We translate our rather complex, primarily global Wholesale Banking, business activities into financial records in line with the latest regulatory and tax requirements. Demand therefore can come from three angles 1) new or changed products/business lines, 2) regulators, central banks and/or tax authorities, and 3) process optimization requests from the end user community. All angles trigger/urge us to analyse the impact and to design, test and implement a solution in the processing chain.
In a nutshell for this role, it is crucial that you have a mindset for taking it on and making it happen, strong analytical capabilities as well as an interest in accountancy, processes, IT and banking products. You will be involved in complex front-to-end initiatives and act as single point of contact from Finance. Next to the coordination activities you will analyse the processes, assess the impact and you will make sure that the business- and user requirements are covered in the change releases. You have a strong drive to learn about the Financial Accounting domain and the tools and techniques under your squad’s responsibility.  Within this position, you have either the possibility to develop yourself into a specialist in a certain domain or to develop to a generic profile with managerial responsibilities.
Who are we looking for?
We are looking for an experienced change expert with a pragmatic mindset that is able to quickly learn about the domain of the squad you will be working in. You get your energy from using your analytical skills to bring complete solutions for the requested change. In this process, you have the capability to quickly build relationships with your stakeholders, both inside and outside your squad. To be able to do this, you have good communication skills. You are able to convincingly put forward proposals and are a real team player in reaching broad agreement on the path to follow.
You are an enthusiastic person that is not afraid to challenge the status quo. With your fresh mindset, you are able to translate external trends into practices that can be implemented within our Tribe.
What you will be doing
As a change expert, you will be working in a constructive, multidisciplinary squad composed of business analysts, engineers and a product owner. Together, you work on Lending and trade initiatives with the objective to onboard new portfolios to the central finance environment and improve the current way of processing and reporting.
Together with your squad members you do everything within your power to realise your common mission day by day. More specifically, this can contain one of the following activities:
Translation of business needs into Finance user and stakeholder needs [requirements];
Act as single point of contact in front-to-end initiatives;
Coordinate and facilitate activities on squad / tribe and/or program level;
You support the product owner and the squad in managing the backlog by translating epics into features and, together with the squad, into user stories;
Information/data analysis: you analyze the necessary input, output, and adjustment of data in the end user processes. You analyze the information need. You investigate the quality of captured data and come up with solutions to improve quality;
Implement and maintain the controls related to minimum accounting standards;
Supporting strategic initiatives to ensure they are delivered in a timely manner – e.g. by executing functional, acceptance and migration testing;
Translate (solution) designs into IT solutions by closely working together with IT;
Your education, experience and skills
You Possess a University (Master’s) degree in (Management) Accounting & Control, Business IT, Accountancy or (Business) economics – having an exceptional academic track record is a plus;
More than five years experience within the financial industry;
Strong analytical and problem solving skills;
Affinity with IT and innovation;
Affinity with the GPC landscape is a plus;
Understanding and knowledge of the banking processes;
Affinity with complex lending products and or trade finance products is a plus;
Knowledge of (Product) Accounting concepts;
Excellent communication skills with the ability to quickly build relationships with your (international) stakeholders;
Knowledge of the Agile way of working is a plus;
You actively ask for help and feedback and are not afraid to give feedback;
Has a customer focus and is result driven;
Team player but also capable of working independently;
Good communication skills in oral and written English.
